45%22%20y%3D%2282%22%20font-size%3D%2213%22%3E2005%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Crect%20x%3D%22625%22%20y%3D%2290%22%20width%3D%2214%22%20height%3D%2214%22%20fill%3D%22%23f59e0b%22%2F%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22645%22%20y%3D%22102%22%20font-size%3D%2213%22%3E2022%3C%2Ftext%3E%3C%2Fg%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E', 'Household recycling rates in five European countries
The percentage of household waste that was recycled in five European countries in 2005 and 2022.
Unit: % of household waste
Series | Germany | Italy | Poland | Spain | UK
2005 | 56 | 22 | 6 | 18 | 27
2022 | 67 | 51 | 40 | 36 | 44
Main features: Recycling rates rose in all five countries. Germany recycled the highest proportion in both years (56% and then 67%) but showed the smallest increase. Poland improved most, from only 6% to 40%, and Italy more than doubled its rate from 22% to 51%, moving ahead of the UK (44%). Spain had the lowest rate in 2022, at 36%.', 'Recycling rates rose in all five countries. Germany recycled the highest proportion in both years (56% and then 67%) but showed the smallest increase. Poland improved most, from only 6% to 40%, and Italy more than doubled its rate from 22% to 51%, moving ahead of the UK (44%). Spain had the lowest rate in 2022, at 36%.'),
