The average number of minutes per day that people in five age groups in the UK spent watching broadcast television and online video in 2023.
Unit: minutes per day
Series | 16-24 | 25-34 | 35-54 | 55-64 | 65+
Broadcast TV | 35 | 70 | 140 | 210 | 290
Online video | 190 | 150 | 95 | 60 | 35
Main features: The two types of viewing moved in opposite directions with age. Broadcast TV viewing rose steadily from 35 minutes a day among 16-24s to 290 minutes among the over-65s, while online video fell from 190 to 35 minutes. The two youngest groups watched more online video than broadcast TV; from 35-54 onwards the reverse was true. Total viewing was highest for the over-65s (325 minutes) and lowest for 25-34s (220 minutes).', 'The two types of viewing moved in opposite directions with age. Broadcast TV viewing rose steadily from 35 minutes a day among 16-24s to 290 minutes among the over-65s, while online video fell from 190 to 35 minutes. The two youngest groups watched more online video than broadcast TV; from 35-54 onwards the reverse was true. Total viewing was highest for the over-65s (325 minutes) and lowest for 25-34s (220 minutes).'),
