The average number of rail journeys made per person in four European countries in 2000, 2010 and 2019.
Unit: journeys per person per year
Series | France | Netherlands | Switzerland | UK
2000 | 17 | 20 | 36 | 13
2010 | 18 | 25 | 43 | 20
2019 | 19 | 27 | 55 | 26
Main features: Rail use increased in all four countries. The Swiss travelled by train far more than people elsewhere, and their figure rose from 36 to 55 journeys a year. The UK figure doubled from 13 to 26, overtaking France by 2010, while France changed very little (17 to 19). The Netherlands rose steadily from 20 to 27.', 'Rail use increased in all four countries. The Swiss travelled by train far more than people elsewhere, and their figure rose from 36 to 55 journeys a year. The UK figure doubled from 13 to 26, overtaking France by 2010, while France changed very little (17 to 19). The Netherlands rose steadily from 20 to 27.'),
