The average weekly rent for a one-bedroom flat in four UK cities in 2015 and 2024.
Unit: £ per week
Series | London | Manchester | Bristol | Glasgow
2015 | 300 | 140 | 175 | 125
2024 | 410 | 210 | 250 | 190
Main features: Rents rose in all four cities. London was by far the most expensive in both years and saw the largest rise in pounds, from £300 to £410 a week. In percentage terms, however, Manchester (£140 to £210) and Glasgow (£125 to £190) rose most, by about half. Bristol remained the second most expensive city and Glasgow the cheapest.', 'Rents rose in all four cities. London was by far the most expensive in both years and saw the largest rise in pounds, from £300 to £410 a week. In percentage terms, however, Manchester (£140 to £210) and Glasgow (£125 to £190) rose most, by about half. Bristol remained the second most expensive city and Glasgow the cheapest.'),
