The percentage of men and women in Australia who took part in five sports or activities at least once a month in 2023.
Unit: % of adults
Series | Walking | Swimming | Cycling | Running | Yoga
Men | 38 | 16 | 14 | 17 | 3
Women | 52 | 18 | 7 | 14 | 16
Main features: Walking was the most popular activity for both sexes, but especially for women (52% compared with 38% of men). The largest differences were in yoga, done by 16% of women but only 3% of men, and cycling, where men were twice as likely to take part (14% and 7%). Swimming and running were similarly popular with men and women.', 'Walking was the most popular activity for both sexes, but especially for women (52% compared with 38% of men). The largest differences were in yoga, done by 16% of women but only 3% of men, and cycling, where men were twice as likely to take part (14% and 7%). Swimming and running were similarly popular with men and women.'),
