The average amount of water used at home per person each day in six countries in 2000 and 2020.
Unit: litres per person per day
Series | US | Australia | Italy | UK | Germany | India
2000 | 380 | 340 | 250 | 150 | 128 | 90
2020 | 310 | 260 | 220 | 142 | 122 | 110
Main features: People in the US used the most water in both years, although use fell by 70 litres to 310. Australia had the largest proportional fall, of about a quarter (340 to 260 litres). Italy fell slightly, while use in the UK and Germany hardly changed. India had the lowest figures and was the only country where use rose (90 to 110 litres).', 'People in the US used the most water in both years, although use fell by 70 litres to 310. Australia had the largest proportional fall, of about a quarter (340 to 260 litres). Italy fell slightly, while use in the UK and Germany hardly changed. India had the lowest figures and was the only country where use rose (90 to 110 litres).'),
