The number of students in England who took A-level exams in five modern languages in 2010 and 2023.
Unit: thousands of students
Series | French | Spanish | German | Chinese | Other languages
2010 | 13 | 7.5 | 5.5 | 2.6 | 6
2023 | 8 | 8.5 | 2.8 | 3.8 | 5.2
Main features: Overall entries fell from 34,600 to 28,300. French was the most popular language in 2010 (13,000) but lost almost 40% of its students and was overtaken by Spanish, which rose to 8,500. German entries roughly halved to 2,800, and Chinese grew from 2,600 to 3,800, moving ahead of German.', 'Overall entries fell from 34,600 to 28,300. French was the most popular language in 2010 (13,000) but lost almost 40% of its students and was overtaken by Spanish, which rose to 8,500. German entries roughly halved to 2,800, and Chinese grew from 2,600 to 3,800, moving ahead of German.'),
