The average time per day that men and women in Canada spent on five types of unpaid work at home in 2022.
Unit: minutes per day
Series | Cooking | Cleaning | Childcare | Shopping | DIY and repairs
Men | 40 | 25 | 30 | 20 | 20
Women | 65 | 55 | 60 | 30 | 5
Main features: Women spent more time than men on every task except DIY and repairs (5 minutes compared with 20). The largest gaps were in cleaning and childcare, where women spent 30 minutes a day more than men, and cooking took the most time for both. In total women did 215 minutes of unpaid work a day, compared with 135 for men.', 'Women spent more time than men on every task except DIY and repairs (5 minutes compared with 20). The largest gaps were in cleaning and childcare, where women spent 30 minutes a day more than men, and cooking took the most time for both. In total women did 215 minutes of unpaid work a day, compared with 135 for men.'),
