The number of passengers using Heathrow, Manchester and Edinburgh airports between 2004 and 2019.
Unit: millions of passengers
Series | 2004 | 2007 | 2010 | 2013 | 2016 | 2019
Heathrow | 67 | 68 | 66 | 72 | 76 | 81
Manchester | 21 | 22 | 17 | 21 | 26 | 29
Edinburgh | 8 | 9 | 9 | 10 | 12 | 15
Main features: Heathrow was much the busiest airport, with passenger numbers rising from 67 to 81 million. All three airports saw little growth or a fall around 2010, most noticeably Manchester, which dropped to 17 million before recovering strongly to 29 million. Edinburgh was the smallest airport but grew fastest in relative terms, almost doubling from 8 to 15 million.', 'Heathrow was much the busiest airport, with passenger numbers rising from 67 to 81 million. All three airports saw little growth or a fall around 2010, most noticeably Manchester, which dropped to 17 million before recovering strongly to 29 million. Edinburgh was the smallest airport but grew fastest in relative terms, almost doubling from 8 to 15 million.'),
