The percentage of new cars sold in Norway that ran on petrol, diesel or electricity between 2012 and 2024.
Unit: % of new cars sold
Series | 2012 | 2014 | 2016 | 2018 | 2020 | 2022 | 2024
Petrol | 55 | 40 | 30 | 25 | 15 | 6 | 2
Diesel | 40 | 45 | 40 | 30 | 15 | 5 | 1
Electric | 3 | 12 | 25 | 40 | 65 | 86 | 95
Main features: Electric cars went from a tiny share of sales (3%) to almost all new cars (95%), becoming the most popular type in 2018. Diesel sales peaked at 45% in 2014 and then fell rapidly, while petrol declined steadily from 55%. By 2024 petrol and diesel together made up only 3% of new cars sold.', 'Electric cars went from a tiny share of sales (3%) to almost all new cars (95%), becoming the most popular type in 2018. Diesel sales peaked at 45% in 2014 and then fell rapidly, while petrol declined steadily from 55%. By 2024 petrol and diesel together made up only 3% of new cars sold.'),
