The value of recorded music sold in the UK in four formats between 2000 and 2024.
Unit: £ millions
Series | 2000 | 2004 | 2008 | 2012 | 2016 | 2020 | 2024
CDs | 1,800 | 1,600 | 1,000 | 600 | 350 | 150 | 120
Downloads | 0 | 60 | 250 | 380 | 200 | 60 | 30
Streaming | 0 | 0 | 10 | 80 | 500 | 1,000 | 1,400
Vinyl | 20 | 10 | 10 | 15 | 60 | 90 | 130
Main features: CDs dominated in 2000 (£1.8 billion) but declined steadily to £120 million. Downloads rose to a peak of £380 million in 2012 and then fell away. Streaming grew from nothing after 2008 to £1.4 billion, overtaking CDs by 2016 and becoming the main format. Vinyl remained small but recovered after 2012 and by 2024 earned slightly more than CDs.', 'CDs dominated in 2000 (£1.8 billion) but declined steadily to £120 million. Downloads rose to a peak of £380 million in 2012 and then fell away. Streaming grew from nothing after 2008 to £1.4 billion, overtaking CDs by 2016 and becoming the main format. Vinyl remained small but recovered after 2012 and by 2024 earned slightly more than CDs.'),
