The number of international tourists who arrived in France, Spain and Thailand between 2000 and 2019.
Unit: millions of arrivals
Series | 2000 | 2005 | 2010 | 2015 | 2019
France | 77 | 75 | 77 | 85 | 90
Spain | 47 | 56 | 53 | 68 | 84
Thailand | 10 | 12 | 16 | 30 | 40
Main features: France received the most tourists throughout, but its numbers were fairly stable until 2010 before rising to 90 million. Spain grew strongly after 2010, from 53 to 84 million, and had almost caught up with France by 2019. Thailand had far fewer arrivals but grew fastest, quadrupling from 10 to 40 million, with the sharpest rise between 2010 and 2015.', 'France received the most tourists throughout, but its numbers were fairly stable until 2010 before rising to 90 million. Spain grew strongly after 2010, from 53 to 84 million, and had almost caught up with France by 2019. Thailand had far fewer arrivals but grew fastest, quadrupling from 10 to 40 million, with the sharpest rise between 2010 and 2015.'),
