The average number of hours of sunshine each month in Brighton and Glasgow.
Unit: hours of sunshine per month
Series | Jan | Feb | Mar | Apr | May | Jun | Jul | Aug | Sep | Oct | Nov | Dec
Brighton | 65 | 85 | 125 | 180 | 225 | 230 | 240 | 220 | 165 | 115 | 75 | 55
Glasgow | 40 | 65 | 100 | 145 | 190 | 170 | 160 | 150 | 115 | 80 | 50 | 35
Main features: Both cities followed the same seasonal pattern, with the least sunshine in December and the most in early summer. Brighton was sunnier in every month and reached its peak of 240 hours in July. Glasgow peaked earlier, at 190 hours in May, and became duller through the summer, so the gap between the cities was widest in July (80 hours).', 'Both cities followed the same seasonal pattern, with the least sunshine in December and the most in early summer. Brighton was sunnier in every month and reached its peak of 240 hours in July. Glasgow peaked earlier, at 190 hours in May, and became duller through the summer, so the gap between the cities was widest in July (80 hours).'),
