2122%22%20font-size%3D%2213%22%3EGermany%3C%2Ftext%3E%3C%2Fg%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E', 'Online share of retail sales in three countries
The percentage of retail sales made online in the UK, China and Germany between 2008 and 2023.
Unit: % of retail sales
Series | 2008 | 2011 | 2014 | 2017 | 2020 | 2023
UK | 5 | 9 | 12 | 16 | 24 | 23
China | 1 | 4 | 11 | 19 | 25 | 28
Germany | 4 | 6 | 8 | 11 | 15 | 14
Main features: The online share of sales grew in every country. At first the UK had the highest share, but China, starting from only 1%, grew fastest and overtook the UK in 2017, reaching 28% by 2023. Germany had the lowest share from 2014 onwards. Both the UK and Germany peaked in 2020 and fell back slightly by 2023.', 'The online share of sales grew in every country. At first the UK had the highest share, but China, starting from only 1%, grew fastest and overtook the UK in 2017, reaching 28% by 2023. Germany had the lowest share from 2014 onwards. Both the UK and Germany peaked in 2020 and fell back slightly by 2023.'),
