20width%3D%2214%22%20height%3D%2214%22%20fill%3D%22%230891b2%22%2F%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22540%22%20y%3D%22374%22%20font-size%3D%2213%22%3EOther%20goods%20and%20services%3C%2Ftext%3E%3C%2Fg%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E', 'How UK households divided their spending
How the average weekly spending of UK households was divided in 1980 and 2020.
1980: Food 22%, Housing 16%, Transport 15%, Recreation 11%, Clothing 9%, Other goods and services 27%
2020: Food 11%, Housing 25%, Transport 15%, Recreation 14%, Clothing 5%, Other goods and services 30%
Main features: The share of spending on housing rose most, from 16% to 25%, making it the largest category in 2020 apart from other goods and services. By contrast, the proportion spent on food halved from 22% to 11% and clothing fell from 9% to 5%. Transport stayed at 15%, recreation rose slightly to 14%, and other goods and services grew from 27% to 30%.', 'The share of spending on housing rose most, from 16% to 25%, making it the largest category in 2020 apart from other goods and services. By contrast, the proportion spent on food halved from 22% to 11% and clothing fell from 9% to 5%. Transport stayed at 15%, recreation rose slightly to 14%, and other goods and services grew from 27% to 30%.'),
