%22362%22%20width%3D%2214%22%20height%3D%2214%22%20fill%3D%22%230891b2%22%2F%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22540%22%20y%3D%22374%22%20font-size%3D%2213%22%3EOther%3C%2Ftext%3E%3C%2Fg%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E', 'Main source of news by age group
The main source of news for adults in three age groups in the UK in 2023.
16-24: Television 15%, Social media 55%, News websites 18%, Radio 5%, Newspapers 2%, Other 5%
35-54: Television 38%, Social media 20%, News websites 25%, Radio 10%, Newspapers 5%, Other 2%
65+: Television 58%, Social media 5%, News websites 10%, Radio 14%, Newspapers 12%, Other 1%
Main features: Social media was the main news source for more than half of 16-24s (55%), while television was the main source for most people over 65 (58%). The middle group used a wider mix, with television (38%), news websites (25%) and social media (20%) all important. Radio and newspapers were more important with age, and newspapers were the main source for 12% of the oldest group but only 2% of the youngest.', 'Social media was the main news source for more than half of 16-24s (55%), while television was the main source for most people over 65 (58%). The middle group used a wider mix, with television (38%), news websites (25%) and social media (20%) all important. Radio and newspapers were more important with age, and newspapers were the main source for 12% of the oldest group but only 2% of the youngest.'),
