0x%3D%22520%22%20y%3D%22362%22%20width%3D%2214%22%20height%3D%2214%22%20fill%3D%22%230891b2%22%2F%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22540%22%20y%3D%22374%22%20font-size%3D%2213%22%3EOther%3C%2Ftext%3E%3C%2Fg%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E', 'Household rubbish collected in Leeds
The make-up of household rubbish collected in Leeds in 2005 and 2023.
2005: Food 25%, Paper and card 28%, Plastics 10%, Glass 10%, Garden waste 15%, Other 12%
2023: Food 32%, Paper and card 18%, Plastics 17%, Glass 6%, Garden waste 12%, Other 15%
Main features: Paper and card made up the largest share of rubbish in 2005 (28%) but fell to 18%, and food waste became the largest category, rising from 25% to 32%. Plastics also increased, from 10% to 17%. The shares of glass and garden waste both fell, while other waste rose slightly.', 'Paper and card made up the largest share of rubbish in 2005 (28%) but fell to 18%, and food waste became the largest category, rising from 25% to 32%. Plastics also increased, from 10% to 17%. The shares of glass and garden waste both fell, while other waste rose slightly.'),
