%22%20font-size%3D%2212%22%20font-weight%3D%22bold%22%20text-anchor%3D%22middle%22%3E3%25%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Crect%20x%3D%2240%22%20y%3D%22340%22%20width%3D%2214%22%20height%3D%2214%22%20fill%3D%22%231d4ed8%22%2F%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%2260%22%20y%3D%22352%22%20font-size%3D%2213%22%3EUnder%2015%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Crect%20x%3D%22280%22%20y%3D%22340%22%20width%3D%2214%22%20height%3D%2214%22%20fill%3D%22%23f59e0b%22%2F%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22300%22%20y%3D%22352%22%20font-size%3D%2213%22%3E15-64%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Crect%20x%3D%22520%22%20y%3D%22340%22%20width%3D%2214%22%20height%3D%2214%22%20fill%3D%22%23059669%22%2F%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22540%22%20y%3D%22352%22%20font-size%3D%2213%22%3E65%20and%20over%3C%2Ftext%3E%3C%2Fg%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E', 'Age structure of Italy and Nigeria
The proportion of the population in three age groups in Italy in 1970 and 2020, and in Nigeria in 2020.
Italy 1970: Under 15 25%, 15-64 64%, 65 and over 11%
Italy 2020: Under 15 13%, 15-64 64%, 65 and over 23%
Nigeria 2020: Under 15 43%, 15-64 54%, 65 and over 3%
Main features: People aged 15-64 made up the majority in every case. Italy’s population aged markedly between 1970 and 2020: the share of children almost halved from 25% to 13%, while the share aged 65 and over doubled to 23%. Nigeria in 2020 had a very young population, with 43% under 15 and only 3% aged 65 and over, and a smaller working-age share (54%) than Italy (64%).', 'People aged 15-64 made up the majority in every case. Italy’s population aged markedly between 1970 and 2020: the share of children almost halved from 25% to 13%, while the share aged 65 and over doubled to 23%. Nigeria in 2020 had a very young population, with 43% under 15 and only 3% aged 65 and over, and a smaller working-age share (54%) than Italy (64%).'),
