The sources of income for a regional theatre in England in 2010 and 2024.
2010: Ticket sales 55%, Government grants 25%, Donations 8%, Café and shop 7%, Other 5%
2024: Ticket sales 60%, Government grants 10%, Donations 12%, Café and shop 13%, Other 5%
Main features: Ticket sales were the main source of income in both years and rose from 55% to 60%. The most significant change was the fall in government grants, from a quarter of income to only 10%. The theatre made up for this with more donations (8% to 12%) and almost doubled the share from its café and shop (7% to 13%).', 'Ticket sales were the main source of income in both years and rose from 55% to 60%. The most significant change was the fall in government grants, from a quarter of income to only 10%. The theatre made up for this with more donations (8% to 12%) and almost doubled the share from its café and shop (7% to 13%).'),
