How undergraduate students at a British university divided their study time in their first year and in their final year.
First year: Lectures 40%, Seminars 15%, Independent study 30%, Group projects 10%, Other 5%
Final year: Lectures 20%, Seminars 12%, Independent study 40%, Group projects 5%, Dissertation research 20%, Other 3%
Main features: First-year students spent the largest share of their study time in lectures (40%), whereas final-year students spent most time on independent study (40%). The share for lectures halved to 20% and group projects also halved, to 5%. Dissertation research, not part of the first year, took a fifth of final-year study time.', 'First-year students spent the largest share of their study time in lectures (40%), whereas final-year students spent most time on independent study (40%). The share for lectures halved to 20% and group projects also halved, to 5%. Dissertation research, not part of the first year, took a fifth of final-year study time.'),
