The population of five large cities in 1950, 1990 and 2020.
City | 1950 (millions) | 1990 (millions) | 2020 (millions)
Tokyo | 11.3 | 32.5 | 37.4
Lagos | 0.3 | 4.8 | 14.4
Mumbai | 3.1 | 12.4 | 20.4
London | 8.4 | 6.8 | 9.3
Mexico City | 3.4 | 15.6 | 21.8
Main features: Tokyo was the largest city at every date and more than tripled to 37.4 million. Lagos grew fastest, from only 0.3 million in 1950, the smallest figure in the table, to 14.4 million. Mumbai and Mexico City both grew roughly six-fold. London was the only city whose population fell, from 8.4 to 6.8 million by 1990, and although it recovered to 9.3 million it was the smallest of the five by 2020.', 'Tokyo was the largest city at every date and more than tripled to 37.4 million. Lagos grew fastest, from only 0.3 million in 1950, the smallest figure in the table, to 14.4 million. Mumbai and Mexico City both grew roughly six-fold. London was the only city whose population fell, from 8.4 to 6.8 million by 1990, and although it recovered to 9.3 million it was the smallest of the five by 2020.'),
