Information about the power, lifespan and costs of four types of light bulb.
Bulb type | Power (watts) | Lifespan (hours) | Price (£) | Running cost per year (£)
Traditional | 60 | 1,000 | 0.80 | 16.00
Halogen | 42 | 2,000 | 1.50 | 11.20
Compact fluorescent | 12 | 8,000 | 3.50 | 3.20
LED | 8 | 25,000 | 4.00 | 2.10
Main features: The traditional bulb was the cheapest to buy (80p) but used the most power, cost the most to run (£16 a year) and had the shortest life. The LED bulb was the most expensive to buy (£4) but used the least power, cost only £2.10 a year to run and lasted 25 times longer. Running costs rose in line with power.', 'The traditional bulb was the cheapest to buy (80p) but used the most power, cost the most to run (£16 a year) and had the shortest life. The LED bulb was the most expensive to buy (£4) but used the least power, cost only £2.10 a year to run and lasted 25 times longer. Running costs rose in line with power.'),
