Information about train services between London and four other British cities.
Route from London | Distance (km) | Fastest journey (minutes) | Standard return fare (£) | Trains per day
Birmingham | 190 | 80 | 95 | 70
Manchester | 300 | 125 | 190 | 48
Cardiff | 245 | 110 | 130 | 34
Edinburgh | 630 | 260 | 160 | 36
Main features: Birmingham was the nearest city, with the shortest journey, the cheapest fare (£95) and by far the most trains (70 a day). Edinburgh was the furthest and took the longest (260 minutes), yet its fare (£160) was lower than the Manchester fare, which was the highest at £190. Cardiff had the fewest trains per day (34).', 'Birmingham was the nearest city, with the shortest journey, the cheapest fare (£95) and by far the most trains (70 a day). Edinburgh was the furthest and took the longest (260 minutes), yet its fare (£160) was lower than the Manchester fare, which was the highest at £190. Cardiff had the fewest trains per day (34).'),
