The average weekly pay and working hours in five occupations in the UK, and the percentage of workers in each who were women.
Occupation | Average weekly pay (£) | Average weekly hours | Women in the job (%)
Nurse | 760 | 37.5 | 89
Software developer | 1,050 | 38 | 20
Bus driver | 620 | 44 | 8
Hairdresser | 390 | 33 | 86
Solicitor | 1,150 | 42 | 55
Main features: Solicitors and software developers earned most (£1,150 and £1,050 a week), while hairdressers earned least (£390) and worked the fewest hours (33). Bus drivers worked the longest week (44 hours) for relatively low pay. Women made up the great majority of nurses (89%) and hairdressers (86%) but only a small minority of software developers (20%) and bus drivers (8%).', 'Solicitors and software developers earned most (£1,150 and £1,050 a week), while hairdressers earned least (£390) and worked the fewest hours (33). Bus drivers worked the longest week (44 hours) for relatively low pay. Women made up the great majority of nurses (89%) and hairdressers (86%) but only a small minority of software developers (20%) and bus drivers (8%).'),
