Information about green space, air quality and cycling in five European capital cities.
City | Green space (% of area) | Days of poor air quality per year | Residents who cycle to work (%)
Copenhagen | 25 | 8 | 45
Amsterdam | 20 | 12 | 38
London | 33 | 35 | 5
Paris | 10 | 42 | 6
Madrid | 15 | 30 | 2
Main features: Copenhagen and Amsterdam had by far the most cyclists (45% and 38%) and the fewest days of poor air (8 and 12). London had the most green space (33%) but a high number of poor-air days (35). Paris had the least green space (10%) and the most days of poor air (42), and Madrid had the fewest people cycling to work (2%).', 'Copenhagen and Amsterdam had by far the most cyclists (45% and 38%) and the fewest days of poor air (8 and 12). London had the most green space (33%) but a high number of poor-air days (35). Paris had the least green space (10%) and the most days of poor air (42), and Madrid had the fewest people cycling to work (2%).'),
