Information about the climate of London, Cardiff, Edinburgh and Belfast.
City | Average July maximum (°C) | Average January minimum (°C) | Annual rainfall (mm) | Days of rain per year
London | 23.5 | 2.4 | 620 | 110
Cardiff | 21.0 | 2.5 | 1,150 | 150
Edinburgh | 19.2 | 1.2 | 700 | 130
Belfast | 18.8 | 2.3 | 950 | 160
Main features: London had the warmest summers (23.5°C) and was the driest city, with the least rain (620 mm) and the fewest rainy days (110). Cardiff received the most rain in total (1,150 mm), but Belfast had the most days of rain (160) and the coolest summers. Winter minimums were similar except in Edinburgh, which was coldest at 1.2°C.', 'London had the warmest summers (23.5°C) and was the driest city, with the least rain (620 mm) and the fewest rainy days (110). Cardiff received the most rain in total (1,150 mm), but Belfast had the most days of rain (160) and the coolest summers. Winter minimums were similar except in Edinburgh, which was coldest at 1.2°C.'),
