%22%20y%3D%22374%22%20font-size%3D%2213%22%3EWater%20sports%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Crect%20x%3D%22280%22%20y%3D%22362%22%20width%3D%2214%22%20height%3D%2214%22%20fill%3D%22%237c3aed%22%2F%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22300%22%20y%3D%22374%22%20font-size%3D%2213%22%3EOther%3C%2Ftext%3E%3C%2Fg%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E%3C%2Fg%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E', 'Visitors to the Lake District National Park
The number of day visitors and staying visitors to the Lake District National Park in each season of 2023, and the pie chart shows the main activity of visitors.
Chart 1 (bar chart): Visitors by season, 2023
Unit: millions of visitors
Series | Spring | Summer | Autumn | Winter
Day visitors | 3.2 | 5.6 | 2.8 | 1.4
Staying visitors | 0.9 | 1.8 | 0.8 | 0.3
Chart 2 (pie chart): Main activity of visitors
All visitors: Walking 45%, Sightseeing by car 20%, Visiting towns and villages 15%, Water sports 10%, Other 10%
Main features: Summer was by far the busiest season, with 7.4 million visitors, and winter the quietest, with 1.7 million. In every season day visitors greatly outnumbered those who stayed overnight, by roughly three to five times. Walking was the main activity for almost half of all visitors (45%), followed by sightseeing by car (20%) and visiting towns and villages (15%).', 'Summer was by far the busiest season, with 7.4 million visitors, and winter the quietest, with 1.7 million. In every season day visitors greatly outnumbered those who stayed overnight, by roughly three to five times. Walking was the main activity for almost half of all visitors (45%), followed by sightseeing by car (20%) and visiting towns and villages (15%).'),
