The number of chain and independent coffee shops in the UK between 2000 and 2020, and the table shows the average price and share of sales of five drinks in 2020.
Chart 1 (line graph): Number of coffee shops
Unit: thousands of shops
Series | 2000 | 2005 | 2010 | 2015 | 2020
Chain shops | 1.5 | 3.5 | 6 | 8.5 | 10
Independent shops | 3 | 4.5 | 5.5 | 7.5 | 8
Chart 2 (table): Drinks sold in coffee shops, 2020
Drink | Average price (£) | Share of sales (%)
Latte | 3.20 | 32
Cappuccino | 3.10 | 24
Americano | 2.70 | 17
Flat white | 3.30 | 15
Tea | 2.20 | 12
Main features: Both kinds of coffee shop increased in number. Independent shops were more common in 2000 (3,000 compared with 1,500), but chains grew faster, overtook them between 2005 and 2010 and reached 10,000 by 2020, against 8,000 independents. Lattes were the most popular drink (32% of sales), followed by cappuccinos (24%). Flat whites were the most expensive (£3.30) and tea the cheapest (£2.20) and least popular (12%).', 'Both kinds of coffee shop increased in number. Independent shops were more common in 2000 (3,000 compared with 1,500), but chains grew faster, overtook them between 2005 and 2010 and reached 10,000 by 2020, against 8,000 independents. Lattes were the most popular drink (32% of sales), followed by cappuccinos (24%). Flat whites were the most expensive (£3.30) and tea the cheapest (£2.20) and least popular (12%).'),
