The types of plastic packaging thrown away by households in the UK in 2022, and the bar chart shows the percentage of each type that was recycled.
Chart 1 (pie chart): Plastic packaging thrown away, by type
2022: Bottles 25%, Pots, tubs and trays 20%, Film and bags 35%, Other 20%
Chart 2 (bar chart): Percentage of each type recycled, 2022
Unit: % recycled
Series | Bottles | Pots, tubs and trays | Film and bags | Other
Recycled | 74 | 45 | 8 | 20
Main features: Film and bags made up the largest share of plastic packaging waste (35%) but had by far the lowest recycling rate, at only 8%. Bottles, a quarter of the waste, were recycled most successfully (74%), and pots, tubs and trays came second (45%). Taken together, only about a third of all plastic packaging was recycled.', 'Film and bags made up the largest share of plastic packaging waste (35%) but had by far the lowest recycling rate, at only 8%. Bottles, a quarter of the waste, were recycled most successfully (74%), and pots, tubs and trays came second (45%). Taken together, only about a third of all plastic packaging was recycled.'),
