The number of bus journeys and car journeys into the city centre in Brighton and Hove between 2005 and 2019, and the pie chart shows the purposes of bus journeys in 2019.
Chart 1 (line graph): Journeys per year
Unit: millions of journeys
Series | 2005 | 2008 | 2011 | 2014 | 2017 | 2019
Bus journeys | 38 | 42 | 45 | 47 | 48 | 49
Car journeys into the centre | 60 | 58 | 55 | 52 | 50 | 48
Chart 2 (pie chart): Purpose of bus journeys, 2019
2019: Work 30%, Shopping 25%, Leisure 20%, Education 15%, Health appointments 5%, Other 5%
Main features: Bus use rose steadily from 38 to 49 million journeys, while car journeys into the centre fell from 60 to 48 million, so that by 2019 buses carried slightly more people than cars. Travelling to work was the most common purpose of bus journeys (30%), followed by shopping (25%) and leisure (20%), with education accounting for 15%.', 'Bus use rose steadily from 38 to 49 million journeys, while car journeys into the centre fell from 60 to 48 million, so that by 2019 buses carried slightly more people than cars. Travelling to work was the most common purpose of bus journeys (30%), followed by shopping (25%) and leisure (20%), with education accounting for 15%.'),
