A village in the south-west of England in 2000 and today.
2000: Main road; Houses; Village shop; Post office; Pub; Primary school; Playing field; Farmland
Today: Main road; Houses; Shop and café; Houses; Pub; Primary school (extended); Playing field; Housing estate; Doctors’ surgery; Car park
Main features: The village has grown considerably, mainly to the south of the main road, where the farmland has been replaced by a housing estate, a doctors’ surgery and a car park. North of the road, the post office has been turned into houses and the village shop now includes a café, while the pub and older houses remain. The primary school has been extended onto part of its playing field.', 'The village has grown considerably, mainly to the south of the main road, where the farmland has been replaced by a housing estate, a doctors’ surgery and a car park. North of the road, the post office has been turned into houses and the village shop now includes a café, while the pub and older houses remain. The primary school has been extended onto part of its playing field.'),
