and%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Crect%20x%3D%22400%22%20y%3D%22294%22%20width%3D%22320%22%20height%3D%2232%22%20fill%3D%22%23e5e7eb%22%20stroke%3D%22%23475569%22%2F%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22560.0%22%20y%3D%22314.0%22%20font-size%3D%2211%22%20text-anchor%3D%22middle%22%3EPath%20and%20cycle%20track%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22706%22%20y%3D%2286%22%20font-size%3D%2213%22%3EN%26%238593%3B%3C%2Ftext%3E%3C%2Fg%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E', 'Changes to a city park in Scotland
A public park in a Scottish city in 1995 and today.
1995: Open grass; Tennis courts; Lake; Bandstand; Flower gardens; Toilets; Car park; Woodland; Main path
Today: Open grass; Children’s play area; Lake; Café; Outdoor gym; Flower gardens; Toilets; Car park; Woodland; Path and cycle track
Main features: The park has been changed to offer more activities. The tennis courts have been replaced by a children’s play area and the bandstand by an outdoor gym. The lake has been made smaller so that a café could be built on its eastern side, and the main path now includes a cycle track. The open grass, flower gardens, toilets, car park and woodland remain as before.', 'The park has been changed to offer more activities. The tennis courts have been replaced by a children’s play area and the bandstand by an outdoor gym. The lake has been made smaller so that a café could be built on its eastern side, and the main path now includes a cycle track. The open grass, flower gardens, toilets, car park and woodland remain as before.'),
