%2Ftext%3E%3C%2Fg%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E', 'The area around a town railway station
The area around the railway station in a town in the north of England in 2005 and today.
2005: Railway line; Platform; Car park; Station building; Taxi rank; Station Road; Empty warehouse; Shops
Today: Railway line; Longer platform; Multi-storey car park; Station building; Cycle hub; Bus and taxi interchange; Station Road; Flats; Shops
Main features: The station area has been redeveloped to improve transport links. The platform has been extended along the whole length of the site, the car park has been replaced by a multi-storey car park, and the taxi rank has been enlarged into a bus and taxi interchange. A cycle hub has been added in front of the station building, and the empty warehouse has been replaced by flats. The station building and shops are unchanged.', 'The station area has been redeveloped to improve transport links. The platform has been extended along the whole length of the site, the car park has been replaced by a multi-storey car park, and the taxi rank has been enlarged into a bus and taxi interchange. A cycle hub has been added in front of the station building, and the empty warehouse has been replaced by flats. The station building and shops are unchanged.'),
