ed into a nature reserve
An area of farmland beside a river in eastern England in 1990 and after it became a nature reserve.
1990: River; Flood bank; Wheat fields; Farmhouse; Cattle grazing; Farm track; Road
Today: River; Reed beds; Flood bank; Lakes and marsh; Bird hides; Visitor centre; Cattle grazing; Footpath; Car park; Road
Main features: The farmland has been turned into a wetland for wildlife. The wheat fields have been flooded to create lakes and marsh, and the western half of the flood bank has been removed and replaced by reed beds. The farmhouse is now a visitor centre, with bird hides beside it, the farm track has become a footpath, and a small car park has been added. Cattle still graze in the south-east of the site.', 'The farmland has been turned into a wetland for wildlife. The wheat fields have been flooded to create lakes and marsh, and the western half of the flood bank has been removed and replaced by reed beds. The farmhouse is now a visitor centre, with bird hides beside it, the farm track has become a footpath, and a small car park has been added. Cattle still graze in the south-east of the site.'),
