The ground floor of a public library in a town in Wales in 2000 and today.
2000: Adult fiction; Reading tables; Non-fiction; Reference books; Newspapers; Children’s books; Reception desk; Entrance
Today: Adult fiction; Café; Non-fiction; Meeting room; Computers; Newspapers and magazines; Children’s books; Self-service machines; Help desk; Entrance
Main features: The library has been reorganised to offer more technology and social space. The reference section has been replaced by computers, the reading tables by a café, and the reception desk by self-service machines, with a small help desk now beside the entrance. The non-fiction area has been reduced to make room for a meeting room, and magazines have been added to the newspaper area. Adult fiction and children’s books are unchanged.', 'The library has been reorganised to offer more technology and social space. The reference section has been replaced by computers, the reading tables by a café, and the reception desk by self-service machines, with a small help desk now beside the entrance. The non-fiction area has been reduced to make room for a meeting room, and magazines have been added to the newspaper area. Adult fiction and children’s books are unchanged.'),
