The process of publishing a new book.
Stage 1: Author sends a draft to a literary agent
Stage 2: Agent offers the book to publishers
Stage 3: Publisher agrees a contract with the author
Stage 4: Editor and author revise the text
Stage 5: Cover designed and pages laid out
Stage 6: Books printed and bound
Stage 7: Books stored in a warehouse
Stage 8: Sent to bookshops and online sellers
Main features: Publishing a book has eight stages. The first three involve finding a publisher through an agent and agreeing a contract. The book is then prepared: the text is revised and the cover and pages are designed. Finally the books are printed, stored and distributed to shops and online sellers.', 'Publishing a book has eight stages. The first three involve finding a publisher through an agent and agreeing a contract. The book is then prepared: the text is revised and the cover and pages are designed. Finally the books are printed, stored and distributed to shops and online sellers.'),
