ill%3D%22%231e3a8a%22%2F%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22234%22%20y%3D%22230%22%20font-size%3D%2212%22%20fill%3D%22%23ffffff%22%20text-anchor%3D%22middle%22%3E7%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22293.0%22%20y%3D%22246%22%20font-size%3D%2212%22%20text-anchor%3D%22middle%22%3EBiodiesel%20washed%20and%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22293.0%22%20y%3D%22261%22%20font-size%3D%2212%22%20text-anchor%3D%22middle%22%3Edried%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Cline%20x1%3D%22218%22%20y1%3D%22255.0%22%20x2%3D%22184%22%20y2%3D%22255.0%22%20stroke%3D%22%231e3a8a%22%20stroke-width%3D%222%22%20marker-end%3D%22url%28%23a%29%22%2F%3E%3Crect%20x%3D%2230%22%20y%3D%22210%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%2290%22%20rx%3D%2210%22%20fill%3D%22%23eff6ff%22%20stroke%3D%22%231e3a8a%22%2F%3E%3Ccircle%20cx%3D%2246%22%20cy%3D%22226%22%20r%3D%2211%22%20fill%3D%22%231e3a8a%22%2F%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%2246%22%20y%3D%22230%22%20font-size%3D%2212%22%20fill%3D%22%23ffffff%22%20text-anchor%3D%22middle%22%3E8%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22105.0%22%20y%3D%22246%22%20font-size%3D%2212%22%20text-anchor%3D%22middle%22%3EBlended%20with%20diesel%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22105.0%22%20y%3D%22261%22%20font-size%3D%2212%22%20text-anchor%3D%22middle%22%3Eand%20sold%20at%20petrol%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22105.0%22%20y%3D%22276%22%20font-size%3D%2212%22%20text-anchor%3D%22middle%22%3Estations%3C%2Ftext%3E%3C%2Fg%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E', 'Turning used cooking oil into fuel
How used cooking oil is turned into biodiesel.
Stage 1: Used oil collected from restaurants
Stage 2: Filtered to remove bits of food
Stage 3: Heated to remove water
Stage 4: Mixed with methanol and a catalyst
Stage 5: Left to separate into two layers
Stage 6: Glycerine layer removed and sold for soap
Stage 7: Biodiesel washed and dried
Stage 8: Blended with diesel and sold at petrol stations
Main features: There are eight stages in turning waste cooking oil into fuel. After collection, the oil is cleaned by filtering and heating, then mixed with methanol and a catalyst. The mixture separates into glycerine, which is sold to make soap, and biodiesel, which is washed, dried and mixed with ordinary diesel before sale.', 'There are eight stages in turning waste cooking oil into fuel. After collection, the oil is cleaned by filtering and heating, then mixed with methanol and a catalyst. The mixture separates into glycerine, which is sold to make soap, and biodiesel, which is washed, dried and mixed with ordinary diesel before sale.'),
