How used plastic drinks bottles are made into fleece jackets.
Stage 1: Bottles collected for recycling
Stage 2: Sorted, and caps and labels removed
Stage 3: Washed in hot water
Stage 4: Shredded into small flakes
Stage 5: Flakes melted and pushed through fine holes
Stage 6: Fibres stretched and spun into yarn
Stage 7: Yarn knitted into fleece fabric
Stage 8: Fabric cut and sewn into jackets
Main features: The process has eight stages and falls into two parts. First the bottles are collected, sorted, cleaned and shredded into flakes. The flakes are then melted and made into fibres, which are spun into yarn, knitted into fleece fabric and finally made into jackets.', 'The process has eight stages and falls into two parts. First the bottles are collected, sorted, cleaned and shredded into flakes. The flakes are then melted and made into fibres, which are spun into yarn, knitted into fleece fabric and finally made into jackets.'),
