fill%3D%22%23eff6ff%22%20stroke%3D%22%231e3a8a%22%2F%3E%3Ccircle%20cx%3D%22234%22%20cy%3D%22226%22%20r%3D%2211%22%20fill%3D%22%231e3a8a%22%2F%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22234%22%20y%3D%22230%22%20font-size%3D%2212%22%20fill%3D%22%23ffffff%22%20text-anchor%3D%22middle%22%3E7%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22293.0%22%20y%3D%22246%22%20font-size%3D%2212%22%20text-anchor%3D%22middle%22%3EStack%20worn%20down%20into%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22293.0%22%20y%3D%22261%22%20font-size%3D%2212%22%20text-anchor%3D%22middle%22%3Ea%20low%20stump%3C%2Ftext%3E%3C%2Fg%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E', 'How sea arches and stacks form
How waves wear away a headland to form caves, arches and stacks.
Stage 1: Waves hit a rocky headland
Stage 2: Water attacks cracks in the rock
Stage 3: Cracks widen into a cave
Stage 4: Cave cut right through to form an arch
Stage 5: Arch roof weakens and falls into the sea
Stage 6: Stack left standing apart from the cliff
Stage 7: Stack worn down into a low stump
Main features: This natural process has seven stages and takes place over a very long time. Waves attack weaknesses in a headland, widening cracks into a cave, which is eventually cut through to make an arch. When the roof of the arch collapses, a separate stack is left, and this is slowly worn down until only a stump remains.', 'This natural process has seven stages and takes place over a very long time. Waves attack weaknesses in a headland, widening cracks into a cave, which is eventually cut through to make an arch. When the roof of the arch collapses, a separate stack is left, and this is slowly worn down until only a stump remains.')
ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

